carrier conclusion
  Euler odd/distinct: binary free choices become odd-shell multiplicities.
  even-graph suspension: binary free choices become parity-completed cycle carriers.
  HYP-2656 CRT/halving: the odd base is rigid; dyadic levels refine it.
  LRC14 reading: bounded AP-tail rows should be routed by odd-shell carry plus
  exact mouth survival before using scalar measure. The unique one-tail
  below-second exception is a pure carry inside an existing odd shell.
  The corrected two-tail minimum introduces a new odd shell and damages
  the old mouth, but already pays the second-value threshold exactly.

